course: dictionary
lesson: 13110
title: A flaw is a fault
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A flaw is a small fault that spoils something, or a weakness in a plan, an argument or a person. Look at the words around it to find its meaning.
explain: «The bowl was lovely, but it had a tiny flaw: a crack near the edge.» The crack spoils the bowl, so a flaw is a fault. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A fault fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: «The plan looked good, but it had a flaw: it needed everyone to be on time.» Here the flaw is a weakness in the plan. Swap in your meaning: a weakness in the plan makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A flaw is a noun: a flaw, flaws.
fact: «Flaw» means a small mark, crack or fault that spoils something.
fact: «Flaw» can also mean a weakness or mistake in a plan, an argument or a person's character.
fact: Phrases to know: «a tiny flaw», «a flaw in the plan», «a fatal flaw».
exercise: «The bowl was lovely, but it had a tiny flaw: a crack near the edge.» What is the flaw here? | A pretty pattern | A bright sunny day | A kind of bowl | *A small fault that spoils the bowl
exercise: «The plan looked good, but it had a flaw: it needed everyone to be on time.» What does flaw mean here? | A long, sunny day | A lovely picture | A reward for a good plan | *A weakness in the plan
exercise: «Her hero was brave, but his temper was his flaw.» Find and copy the word that names the weakness. | hero | *temper | his | brave
test: «A flaw in the test made the result untrustworthy.» What does the flaw do to the test? | It makes the result easy to trust | It makes the test longer | It hides the result | *It spoils the test, so the result cannot be fully trusted
test: Which phrase means a serious weakness that could ruin everything? | a tiny flaw | a shiny flaw | a flaw in the picture | *a fatal flaw
exam: The hero's flaw was a temper that caused trouble. What is a flaw? | A brave deed | A wise saying | A tiny sound | *A weakness or mistake in a character
